First things first, in order to understand this part, you need a bit context, ‘kay
Hollow Knight is a Metroidvania style video game released by Team Cherry on February 24th 2017
It has been praised for its unique gameplay and extremely difficult boss battles, of which MANY occur
About 2 years later, in 2019 I think, the sequel/spin-off game Hollow Knight: Silksong was once announced
In it, you play as Hornet, one of the bosses you encounter while playing HW and a fan-fav, and the gameplay is the same
The fans were eagerly waiting for Silksong to come out, but even after 4 years and one massive pandemic, there was no confirmed signs of it manifesting
The community was getting desperate, to the point where they started Silkposting in false hope 
and even sacrificing members of their sub-reddit to their doom (virtually, of course)

Finally, in late August this year, the trailer for Silksong dropped and the game was announced to release on Steam on September 4th
Unfortunately for me, I was attending classes that day, so I couldn’t really join in, but the turnout was amazing
Within the first 45 minutes of it being released, 100,000 players were playing consecutively, 
making it the 10th most played game upon release in Steam history
