Anyways, while just about one of the most anticipated games came out yesterday, meanwhile, the Funkin’ Crew had something planned
The 0.7.4 update was released on Labor day (fitting, considering it a national holiday) and it changed a lot
It has been referred to by Hundrec as one of the best patches of FNF and honestly, I frickin’ agree
This hotfix patch has everything, from game optimization, album changes, and the mandatory charting issues fixed, of course
If you want a full changelog of what’s happened, check the Funkin Crew’s Github page, but lemme cover the “big” ones real quick:

A new transition screen was added for freeplay and the weeks transition (a very cool fade out, now I kinda want the fade in too)
Haptics (basically phone vibrations) were added for the can explosions in 2Hot for Mobile (makes the game more life-like, also cool)
There are now 2 new animations that play in “Attract Mode”, if you let the game idle for enough time 
(these are the Boyfriend Everywhere commercial and the FNF Mobile Trailer)
Camera Zoom inputs can now be customized to be timed to the beat of whatever song you want (a huge change for those using the built-in chart editor)
If you get a Sick! Note, the splash effect is now centered (as compared to it being off-kilter, overall very nice)
Monster and Winter Horrorland have the correct albums listed under freeplay (some people were annoyed by this, me not included)
The idle time for Stress and Roses has now been properly removed (good, that was bugging me for sure)
There is now a Hey! Animation for BF’s christmas sprites (A huge change to those using the animation editor sprites)
Stress (Pico mix) no longer restarts after you’ve played through the song once (this one went past the milestone due date, might’ve been a problem on client-side, I think)
And a whole bunch of charting issues were fixed, like a butt-TON

So yeah, those are just some of the changes for FNF’s 0.7.4 update, which released over Labor Day weekend
Now, due to some reviewing on Google Play’s part, the update did not arrive for Android until September 3rd, but whatever, it’s there now
Happy playing, y’all, remember to get your funk on
It helps if you use two hands (that’s right, I’ve switched over) and I have a really special technique
You use the left hand to press the A and S keys and your right hand to press the up and right keys
This way, your hands are spread on the keyboard and you can catch all possible note patterns
As for fingers to use, I use my ring and middle fingers to press the keys for both hands
This method is extremely effective, as it helped me complete Stress (Pico Mix) with an E score (I no longer struggle there, yeah!)
It also helped me to, as of today, get a P on Fresh(Nightmare) TODAY, which is huge
I’m not usually meticulous on whether or not I get a perfect rating on a song, but I just had to do it, considering I missed only a note yesterday
No, I’m not gonna get a golden P or, as the Funk-modders would say, FC the song, I’ll take my Perfect rating in whatever form

